From 191633fb53deab49f7e3361065cb1ba19574127f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Max (Muse)" <max@local.prototype>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 17:24:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Prototype time-capsule mode: pick a simulation date at
 login

- New cis_timecapsule module: featured dates, 1979-1998 range,
  MM/DD/YYYY validation, deterministic surprise dates (content packs stubbed)
- SessionState gains simulation_date (no new module-level globals);
  cis_session.active_session/current_session_state/session_simulation_date
  expose it via ContextVar (process-per-session keeps it session-scoped)
- simulation_day() prefers the session date, else existing env/default behavior
- Temporal destination screen runs once after login, before the main menu:
  present day / featured dates / manual entry / surprise me, plus a
  'Return to <date>?' shortcut persisted per account in profiles.json
- Post-login briefing shows the chosen date with a dynamic year title and
  falls back to on-this-day history outside the 1988 archive; period news
  and CB ambience inherit per-date determinism via the existing seeded rng()
- Works over console, web, and telnet (all spawn compuserve.py per session)
- Adds TimeCapsuleTests (6 tests); suite: 179/180 pass, sole failure is the
  known pre-existing date-flaky chip-88 test
