From 9eeee5dbe40eaa3e72b1365a5d21438c89e72879 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Max (Muse)" <max@local.prototype>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 17:31:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Time-capsule content packs: curated archival content for
 all six featured dates

Adds timecapsule_packs.json with hand-written, wire-service-voice packs for
1981-08-12 (IBM PC), 1984-01-24 (Macintosh), 1986-01-28 (Challenger),
1987-10-19 (Black Monday), 1989-11-09 (Berlin Wall), and 1991-08-06 (first
public Web invitation). Each pack holds 8-12 archival headlines, 2-4 service
announcements, 4-6 CB topics, 0-4 market notes, and 2-3 on-this-day items,
all researched from real events of the date/week with zero anachronisms.

Wiring:
- cis_timecapsule: validated JSON loader (mirrors cis_timeline), pack_for(),
  pack_headlines(), cb_conversation(); CONTENT_PACK_STATUS now 'loaded'.
- compuserve.period_news_edition(): featured dates get their archival wire
  edition with a date-aware banner instead of the December-1988 edition.
- compuserve.today_in_1988_lines(): briefing gains ARCHIVAL HEADLINES,
  MARKET WIRE, and SERVICE ANNOUNCEMENTS sections; pack on-this-day items
  take precedence in TODAY IN HISTORY.
- cis_dynamic.cb_ambient_events(): 35% of ambient CB chatter on featured
  dates comes from the pack's topics, paired with period handles.

Challenger coverage is grave and respectful throughout. Adds 8 tests;
full suite 187/188 (only the known pre-existing flaky CHIP-88 failure,
verified against the base commit); smoke_test.py passes.
